{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_011QmL6iy2E6Xiw1fSZx5Sje","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have all the key KB documents:\n- `EMPTY-KB.md` - explicitly states it contains no bibliographic evidence and should not be cited\n- `T1.compile.research.md` - contains SLOTS about standards and guidance, charge windows - NOT directly relevant to EEMD filtering, but has some good context about blast vibration\n- `T3.compile.research.md` - contains all 5 slots directly relevant to EEMD/EMD filtering and reconstruction - this is the primary KB source\n\nThe task requires me to write T9.research.md with 5 slots:\n1. Authoritative EMD/EEMD Filtering References\n2. Supported Component Removal Practices\n3. Known Limitations To Report\n4. Validation Checks For EEMD-Filtered Histories\n5. Description Without Overclaiming\n\nT3 has detailed content for all five slots, and I need to preserve the citekeys [@Ref001] through [@Ref011] exactly as they appear in the source material.\n\nNow I'm doing an external research pass to complement what's in the KB. T3 covers the topic well across all slots, but I should validate with external sources and check for any gaps. The key foundational references I'm tracking are the original EMD work by Huang et al. from 1998, the EEMD extension by Wu and Huang in 2009, and the 2004 paper by Flandrin, Rilling, and Goncalves on mode mixing issues. I need to follow the workflow instructions more carefully—preserving the [@Key] citekeys from T3.compile.research.md rather than collapsing them, adding [KB:T3.compile.research.md] tokens where I retain passages, and searching for external sources to fill gaps while keeping all citations in their token forms without converting them. Now I'll search Zotero for the key EEMD and signal processing papers, and also do web searches to fill any gaps, particularly around engineering applications to blast vibration.","signature":""}],"stop_