{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MeYHFNFJAB9sJvuzdGyEEZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Wu Huang 2009 \"ensemble empirical mode decomposition\" noise-assisted DOI\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Ensemble empirical mode decomposition: A noise-assisted data analysis method - National Central University\",\"url\":\"https://scholars.ncu.edu.tw/en/publications/ensemble-empirical-mode-decomposition-a-noise-assisted-data-analy/\"},{\"title\":\"Ensemble empirical mode decomposition: A noise-assisted data analysis method - National Yang Ming Chiao Tung University Academic Hub\",\"url\":\"https://scholar.nycu.edu.tw/en/publications/ensemble-empirical-mode-decomposition-a-noise-assisted-data-analy/\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Ensemble empirical mode decomposition: a noise-assisted data analysis method (2009) | Zhaohua Wu | 8020 Citations\",\"url\":\"https://scispace.com/papers/ensemble-empirical-mode-decomposition-a-noise-assisted-data-4htvj7tcuy\"},{\"title\":\"Wu, Z. and Huang, N.E. (2009) Ensemble Empirical Mode Decomposition A Noise-Assisted Data Analysis Method. Advances in Adaptive Data Analysis, 1, 1-41. - References - Scientific Research Publishing\",\"url\":\"https://www.scirp.org/reference/referencespapers?referenceid=2995657\"},{\"title\":\"Wu, Z. H., & Huang, N. E. (2009). Ensemble Empirical Mode Decomposition A Noise-assisted Data Analysis Method. Advances in Adaptive Data Analysis, 1, 1-41. - References - Scientific Research Publishing\",\"url\":\"https://www.scirp.org/reference/referencespapers?referenceid=1578606\"},{\"title\":\"Wu, Z.H. and Huang, N.E. (2009) Ensemble Empirical Mode Decomposi-tion A Noise Assisted Data Analysis Method. Advances in Adaptive Data Analysis, 1, 1-41. - References - Scientific Research Publishing\",\"url\":\"https://www.scirp.org/reference/referencespapers?referenceid=2096568\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) COMPLEMENTARY ENSEMBLE EMPIRICAL MODE DECOMPOSITION: A NOVEL NOISE ENHANCED DATA ANALYSIS METHOD\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/14188927/COMPLEMENTARY_ENSEMBLE_EMPIRICAL_MODE_DECOMPOSITION_A_NOVEL_NOISE_ENHANCED_DATA_ANALYSIS_METHOD\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Complementary Ensemble Empirical Mode Decomposition: a Novel Noise Enhanced Data Analysis Method.\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220531136_Complementary_Ensemble_Empirical_Mode_Decomposition_a_Novel_Noise_Enhanced_Data_Analysis_Method\"},{\"title\":\"Ensemble Empirical Mode Decomposition: a Noise-Assisted Data Analysis Method | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220531146_Ensemble_Empirical_Mode_Decomposition_a_Noise-Assisted_Data_Analysis_Method\"},{\"title\":\"Preliminary experimental results of determining the geopotential   difference between two synchronized portable hydrogen clocks at different   locations\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2008.06271\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here is the information about the Wu and Huang 2009 paper on Ensemble Empirical Mode Decomposition:\n\n**Publication Details:**\n\nWu Z and Huang NE published \"Ensemble empirical mode decomposition: A noise-assisted data analysis method\" in Advances in Adaptive Data Analysis in January 2009, Volume 1, Issue 1, pages 1-41, with DOI: 10.1142/S1793536909000047.\n\n**Overview:**\n\nThe paper presents a new Ensemble Empirical Mode Decomposition (EEMD) approach that consists of sifting an ensemble of white noise-added signal (data) and treats the mean as the final true result. Finite, not infinitesimal, amplitude white noise is necessary to force the ensemble to exhaust all possible solutions in the sifting process, thus making the different scale signals to collate in the proper intrinsic mode functions (IMF) dictated by the dyadic filter banks.\n\nThe DOI for this paper is **10.1142/S1793536909000047** or **https://doi.org/10.1142/S1793536909000047**.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9958eae5-5a95-4e8c-919f-b61a93167db8","uuid":"a32e7fcc-b25a-4702-852f-8293971e9d52","timestamp":"2026-07-06T20:44:48.072Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Wu Huang 2009 \"ensemble empirical mode decomposition\" noise-assisted DOI","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_013Gf2jCEVVmVWsUXzLHEATi","content":[{"title":"Ensemble empirical mode decomposition: A noise-assisted data analysis method - National Central University","url":"https://scholars.ncu.edu.tw/en/publications/ensemble-empirical-mode-decomposition-a-noise-assisted-data-analy/"},{"title":"Ensemble empirical mode decomposition: A noise-assisted data analysis method - National Yang Ming Chiao Tung University Academic Hub","url":"https://scholar.nycu.edu.tw/en/publications/ensemble-empirical-mode-decomposition-a-noise-assisted-data-analy/"},{"title":"(PDF) Ensemble empirical mode decomposition: a noise-assisted data analysis method (2009) | Zhaohua Wu | 8020 Citations","url":"https://scispace.com/papers/ensemble-empirical-mode-decomposition-a-noise-assisted-data-4htvj7tcuy"},{"title":"Wu, Z. and Huang, N.E. (2009) Ensemble Empirical Mode Decomposition A Noise-Assisted Data Analysis Method. Advances in Adaptive Data Analysis, 1, 1-41. - References - Scientific Research Publishing","url":"https://www.scirp.org/reference/referencespapers?referenceid=2995657"},{"title":"Wu, Z. H., & Huang, N. E. (2009). Ensemble Empirical Mode Decomposition A Noise-assisted Data Analysis Method. Advances in Adaptive Data Analysis, 1, 1-41. - References - Scientific Research Publishing","url":"https://www.scirp.org/reference/referencespapers?referenceid=1578606"},{"title":"Wu, Z.H. and Huang, N.E. (2009) Ensemble Empirical Mode Decomposi-tion A Noise Assisted Data Analysis Method. Advances in Adaptive Data Analysis, 1, 1-41. - References - Scientific Research Publishing","url":"https://www.scirp.org/reference/referencespapers?referenceid=2096568"},{"title":"(PDF) COMPLEMENTARY ENSEMBLE EMPIRICAL MODE DECOMPOSITION: A NOVEL NOISE ENHANCED DATA ANALYSIS METHOD","url":"https://www.academia.edu/14188927/COMPLEMENTARY_ENSEMBLE_EMPIRICAL_MODE_DECOMPOSITION_A_NOVEL_NOISE_ENHANCED_DATA_ANALYSIS_METHOD"},{"title":"(PDF) Complementary Ensemble Empirical Mode Decomposition: a Novel Noise Enhanced Data Analysis Method.","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220531136_Complementary_Ensemble_Empirical_Mode_Decomposition_a_Novel_Noise_Enhanced_Data_Analysis_Method"},{"title":"Ensemble Empirical Mode Decomposition: a Noise-Assisted Data Analysis Method | Request PDF","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220531146_Ensemble_Empirical_Mode_Decomposition_a_Noise-Assisted_Data_Analysis_Method"},{"title":"Preliminary experimental results of determining the geopotential   difference between two synchronized portable hydrogen clocks at different   locations","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2008.06271"}]},"Based on the search results, here is the information about the Wu and Huang 2009 paper on Ensemble Empirical Mode Decomposition:\n\n**Publication Details:**\n\nWu Z and Huang NE published \"Ensemble empirical mode decomposition: A noise-assisted data analysis method\" in Advances in Adaptive Data Analysis in January 2009, Volume 1, Issue 1, pages 1-41, with DOI: 10.1142/S1793536909000047.\n\n**Overview:**\n\nThe paper presents a new Ensemble Empirical Mode Decomposition (EEMD) approach that consists of sifting an ensemble of white noise-added signal (data) and treats the mean as the final true result. Finite, not infinitesimal, amplitude white noise is necessary to force the ensemble to exhaust all possible solutions in the sifting process, thus making the different scale signals to collate in the proper intrinsic mode functions (IMF) dictated by the dyadic filter banks.\n\nThe DOI for this paper is **10.1142/S1793536909000047** or **https://doi.org/10.1142/S1793536909000047**."],"durationSeconds":6.233594416,"searchCount":1}}
