 Tung, Henry H. Liu\n\n**Title:** \"The empirical mode decomposition and the Hilbert spectrum for nonlinear and non-stationary time series analysis\" - A new method for analysing nonlinear and non-stationary data with the empirical mode decomposition method that decomposes complicated data sets into intrinsic mode functions that admit well-behaved Hilbert transforms.\n\n**Publication:** Proceedings of the Royal Society A, March 1, 1998, Volume 454, Issue 1971, pages 903–995\n\n**DOI:** https://doi.org/10.1098/rspa.1998.0193"],"durationSeconds":5.894272791999989,"searchCount":1}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012xzPXkUeG74NWnaKTYjcVZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Kopsinis McLaughlin 2009 \"enhanced empirical mode decomposition\" denoising IMF DOI\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A Gyroscope Signal Denoising Method Based on Empirical Mode Decomposition and Signal Reconstruction - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6928915/\"},{\"title\":\"Denoising the ECG Signal Using Ensemble Empirical Mode Decomposition | Engineering, Technology & Applied Science Research\",\"url\":\"https://www.etasr.com/index.php/ETASR/article/view/4302\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Empirical Mode Decomposition in Discrete Time Signals Denoising\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/105691146/Empirical_Mode_Decomposition_in_Discrete_Time_Signals_Denoising\"},{\"title\":\"Relevant modes selection method based on Spearman correlation coefficient for laser signal denoising using empirical mode decomposition | Optical Review | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10043-016-0275-x\"},{\"title\":\"Development of EMD-based denoising methods inspired by wavelet thresholding | IEEE Transactions on Signal Processing\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1109/tsp.2009.2013885\"},{\"title\":\"An integrated EMD adaptive threshold denoising method for reduction of noise in ECG | PLOS One\",\"url\":\"https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371%2Fjournal.pone.0235330\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) EMPIRICAL MODE DECOMPOSITION BASED DENOISING TECHNIQUES\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/241523693_EMPIRICAL_MODE_DECOMPOSITION_BASED_DENOISING_TECHNIQUES\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] EMPIRICAL MODE DECOMPOSITION BASED DENOISING TECHNIQUES | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/EMPIRICAL-MODE-DECOMPOSITION-BASED-DENOISING-Kopsinis/8c25a1f7c2935579136a41bd32bf7e63fd6d02ac\"},{\"title\":\"Speech Denoising Based on Empirical Mode Decomposition and Improved Thresholding | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/299709982_Speech_Denoising_Based_on_Empirical_Mode_Decomposition_and_Improved_Thresholding\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the Kopsinis and McLaughlin 2009 paper on EMD-based denoising:\n\nThe paper is titled \"Development of EMD-Based Denoising Methods Inspired by Wavelet Thresholding,\" published in IEEE Transactions on Signal Processing, vol. 57, no. 4, pp. 1351-1362, April 2009, with DOI: https://doi.org/10.1109/TSP.2009.2013885.\n\nKopsinis and McLaughlin developed an enhanced strategy for signal denoising using EMD, inspired by the wavelet thresholding method, where hard and soft thresholding techniques were revisited and a new thresholding method called interval thresholding was proposed to improve the effectiveness of the denoising.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9958eae5-5a95-4e8c-919f-b61a93167db8","uuid":"786714c9-d828-4cc7-8f93-4ad4e116986e","timestamp":"2026-07-06T20:45:02.468Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Kopsinis McLaughlin 2009 \"enhanced empirical mode decomposition\" denoising IMF DOI","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01KDpJMzRZ3vo23hNTT3NWvq","content":[{"title":"A Gyroscope Signal Denoising Method Based on Empirical Mode Decomposition and Signal Reconstruction - PMC","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6928915/"},{"title":"Denoising the ECG Signal Using Ensemble Empirical Mode Decomposition | Engineering, Technology & Applied Science Research","url":"https://www.etasr.com/index.php/ETASR/article/view/4302"},{"title":"(PDF) Empirical Mode Decomposition in Discrete Time Signals Denoising","url":"https://www.academia.edu/105691146/Empirical_Mode_Decomposition_in_Discrete_Time_Signals_Denoising"},{"title":"Relevant modes selection method based on Spearman correlation coefficient for laser signal denoising using empirical mode decomposition | Optical Review | Springer Nature Link","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10043-016-0275-x"},{"title":"Development of EMD-based denoising methods inspired by wavelet thresholding | IEEE Transactions on Signal Processing","url":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1109/tsp.2009.2013885"},{"title":"An integrated EMD adaptive threshold denoising method for reduction of noise in ECG | PLOS One","url":"https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371%2Fjournal.pone.0235330"},{"title":"(PDF) EMPIRICAL MODE DECOMPOSITION BASED DENOISING TECHNIQUES","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/241523693_EMPIRICAL_MODE_DECOMPOSITION_BASED_DENOISING_TECHNIQUES"},{"title":"[PDF] EMPIRICAL MODE DECOMPOSITION BASED DENOISING TECHNIQUES | Semantic Scholar","url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/EMPIRICAL-MODE-DECOMPOSITION-BASED-DENOISING-Kopsinis/8c25a1f7c2935579136a41bd32bf7e63fd6d02ac"},{"title":"Speech Denoising Based on Empirical Mode Decomposition and Improved Thresholding | Request PDF","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/299709982_Speech_Denoising_Based_on_Empirical_Mode_Decomposition_and_Improved_Thresholding"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about the Kopsinis and McLaughlin 2009 paper on EMD-based denoising:\n\nThe paper is titled \"Development of EMD-Based Denoising Methods Inspired by Wavelet Thresholding,\" published in IEEE Transactions on Signal Processing, vol. 57, no. 4, pp. 1351-1362, April 2009, with DOI: https://doi.org/10.1109/TSP.2009.2013885.\n\nKopsinis and McLaughlin developed an enhanced strategy for signal denoising using EMD, inspired by the wavelet thresholding method, where hard and soft thresholding techniques were revisited and a new thresholding method called interval thresholding was proposed to improve the effectiveness of the denoising."],"durationSeconds":5.1490783749999975,"searchCount":1}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SwMX8hJupXzUpqFB6qm6a2","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Boore Bommer 2005 \"processing of strong-motion accelerograms\" DOI journal\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Processing of strong-motion accelerograms: Needs, options and consequences\",\"url\":\"https://pubs.usgs.gov/publication/70029089\"},{\"title\":\"Processing of strong-motion accelerograms: needs, options and consequences\",\"url\":\"http://www.daveboore.com/pubs_online/record_processing_sdee_final.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Effects of Digital Filtering in Data Processing of Seismic Acceleration Records | EURASIP Journal on Advances in Signal Processing | Full Text\",\"url\":\"https://asp-eurasipjournals.springeropen.com/articles/10.1155/2007/29502\"},{\"title\":\"Processing of strong-motion accelerograms: Needs, options and consequences | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/222425169_Processing_of_strong-motion_accelerograms_Needs_options_and_consequences\"},{\"title\":\"Strong-motion processing service: a tool to access and analyse earthquakes strong-motion waveforms | Bulletin of Earthquake Engineering | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10518-017-0299-z\"},{\"title\":\"Figure 25 from Processing of strong-motion accelerograms: needs, options and consequences | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Processing-of-strong-motion-accelerograms:-needs,-Boore-Bommer/007939bac686d36b7a85f28c8e3d931313c846aa/figure/24\"},{\"title\":\"Google Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?title=Processing+of+strong-motion+accelerograms:+Needs,+options+and+consequences&amp=&author=D.+M.+Boore&amp=&author=J.+J.+Bommer&amp=&publication_year=2005&amp=&journal=Soil+Dyn.+Earthquake+Eng.&amp=&pages=93-115&amp=&doi=10.1016/j.soildyn.2004.10.007\"},{\"title\":\"Processing of strong-motion accelerograms: needs, options and consequences - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0267726104001708\"},{\"title\":\"Elasto-acoustic modelling and simulation for the seismic response of   structures: The case of the Tahtal{\\\\i} dam in the 2020 \\\\.Izmir earthquake\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2110.15875\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here is the information about the Boore and Bommer 2005 paper on processing strong-motion accelerograms:\n\n**Publication Details:**\n\nThe paper titled \"Processing of strong-motion accelerograms: Needs, options and consequences\" was published by Boore and Bommer in 2005 in Soil Dynamics and Earthquake Engineering, volume 25, number 2, pages 93-115, with DOI: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.soildyn.2004.10.007\n\n**Journal:** Soil Dynamics and Earthquake Engineering\n\n**Authors:** David M. Boore and Julian J. Bommer\n\nThis is a foundational work in the field of earthquake engineering. Recordings from strong-motion accelerographs are of fundamental importance in earthquake engineering, forming the basis for all characterizations of ground shaking employed for seismic design. The recordings, particularly those from analog instruments, invariably contain noise that can mask and distort the ground-motion signal at both high and low frequencies, and for any application of recorded accelerograms, it is important to identify the presence of this noise in the digitized time-history and its influence on the parameters that are to be derived from the records.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9958eae5-5a95-4e8c-919f-b61a93167db8","uuid":"138709c9-cadb-4138-830a-c200092b1385","timestamp":"2026-07-06T20:45:02.846Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Boore Bommer 2005 \"processing of strong-motion accelerograms\" DOI journal","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01K8thB8bAN2BNgKApmMFbCt","content":[{"title":"Processing of strong-motion accelerograms: Needs, options and consequences","url":"https://pubs.usgs.gov/publication/70029089"},{"title":"Processing of strong-motion accelerograms: needs, options and consequences","url":"http://www.daveboore.com/pubs_online/record_processing_sdee_final.pdf"},{"title":"Effects of Digital Filtering in Data Processing of Seismic Acceleration Records | EURASIP Journal on Advances in Signal Processing | Full Text","url":"https://asp-eurasipjournals.springeropen.com/articles/10.1155/2007/29502"},{"title":"Processing of strong-motion accelerograms: Needs, options and consequences | Request PDF","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/222425169_Processing_of_strong-motion_accelerograms_Needs_options_and_consequences"},{"title":"Strong-motion processing service: a tool to access and analyse earthquakes strong-motion waveforms | Bulletin of Earthquake Engineering | Springer Nature Link","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10518-017-0299-z"},{"title":"Figure 25 from Processing of strong-motion accelerograms: needs, options and consequences | Semantic Scholar","url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Processing-of-strong-motion-accelerograms:-needs,-Boore-Bommer/007939bac686d36b7a85f28c8e3d931313c846aa/figure/24"},{"title":"Google Scholar","url":"https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?title=Processing+of+strong-motion+accelerograms:+Needs,+options+and+consequences&amp=&author=D.+M.+Boore&amp=&author=J.+J.+Bommer&amp=&publication_year=2005&amp=&journal=Soil+Dyn.+Earthquake+Eng.&amp=&pages=93-115&amp=&doi=10.1016/j.soildyn.2004.10.007"},{"title":"Processing of strong-motion accelerograms: needs, options and consequences - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0267726104001708"},{"title":"Elasto-acoustic modelling and simulation for the seismic response of   structures: The case of the Tahtal{\\i} dam in the 2020 \\.Izmir earthquake","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2110.15875"}]},"Based on the search results, here is the information about the Boore and Bommer 2005 paper on processing strong-motion accelerograms:\n\n**Publication Details:**\n\nThe paper titled \"Processing of strong-motion accelerograms: Needs, options and consequences\" was published by Boore and Bommer in 2005 in Soil Dynamics and Earthquake Engineering, volume 25, number 2, pages 93-115, with DOI: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.soildyn.2004.10.007\n\n**Journal:** Soil Dynamics and Earthquake Engineering\n\n**Authors:** David M. Boore and Julian J. Bommer\n\nThis is a foundational work in the field of earthquake engineering. Recordings from strong-motion accelerographs are of fundamental importance in earthquake engineering, forming the basis for all characterizations of ground shaking employed for seismic design. The recordings, particularly those from analog instruments, invariably contain noise that can mask and distort the ground-motion signal at both high and low frequencies, and for any application of recorded accelerograms, it is important to identify the presence of this noise in the digitized time-history and its influence on the parameters that are to be derived from the records."],"durationSeconds":5.948085041999992,"searchCount":1}}
