{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JtZjCLAgah1C9mDKfCYwvi","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Boudraa Cexus 2007 \"EMD-based signal filtering using Teager energy operator\" DOI IEEE\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"dblp: Abdel-Ouahab Boudraa\",\"url\":\"https://dblp.uni-trier.de/pers/hd/b/Boudraa:Abdel=Ouahab\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) EMD-Based Signal Filtering\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/17726709/EMD_Based_Signal_Filtering\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) EMD-Based Signal Noise Reduction\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/228999069_EMD-Based_Signal_Noise_Reduction\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] EMD-Based Signal Filtering | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/EMD-Based-Signal-Filtering-Boudraa-Cexus/e4d3324e318ed6531ebe8d0d03b0fbe94ad6fba3\"},{\"title\":\"Application of a variation of empirical mode decomposition and teager energy operator to EEG signals for mental task classification | ScienceGate\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencegate.app/document/10.1109/embc.2013.6609663\"},{\"title\":\"Ensemble Empirical Mode Decomposition-Based Teager Energy Spectrum for Bearing Fault Diagnosis | Journal of Vibration and Acoustics | ASME Digital Collection\",\"url\":\"https://asmedigitalcollection.asme.org/vibrationacoustics/article-abstract/135/3/031013/472379/Ensemble-Empirical-Mode-Decomposition-Based-Teager?redirectedFrom=fulltext\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Nonstationary signals analysis by Teager-Huang Transform (THT)\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/47760351_Nonstationary_signals_analysis_by_Teager-Huang_Transform_THT\"},{\"title\":\"Multicomponent AM–FM signals analysis based on EMD–B-splines ESA - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0165168412000692\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) EMD-Based signal filtering\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220409465_EMD-Based_signal_filtering\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Signal detection based on empirical mode decomposition and Teager–Kaiser energy operator and its application to P and S wave arrival time detection in seismic signal analysis\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/38207719/Signal_detection_based_on_empirical_mode_decomposition_and_Teager_Kaiser_energy_operator_and_its_application_to_P_and_S_wave_arrival_time_detection_in_seismic_signal_analysis\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the paper you're looking for:\n\nThe paper \"EMD-Based Signal Filtering\" by Abdel-Ouahab Boudraa and Jean-Christophe Cexus was published in IEEE Transactions on Instrumentation and Measurement, volume 56, issue 6, pages 2196-2202 in 2007.\n\nThe paper proposes a method using partial reconstructions of the signal with relevant Intrinsic Mode Functions (IMFs) corresponding to the most important structures of the signal, with a criterion to determine when the energy distribution of important signal structures overcomes that of noise and high-frequency components.\n\nHowever, the search results do not provide the specific DOI number for this publication. To obtain the complete DOI, you may want to search directly on IEEE Xplore or the paper's direct publication page.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9958eae5-5a95-4e8c-919f-b61a93167db8","uuid":"5d7f8ae5-af60-4fa6-8f64-0b42a7244126","timestamp":"2026-07-06T20:45:18.396Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Boudraa Cexus 2007 \"EMD-based signal filtering using Teager energy operator\" DOI IEEE","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01R89g9mu772fggyBdzN6n8d","content":[{"title":"dblp: Abdel-Ouahab Boudraa","url":"https://dblp.uni-trier.de/pers/hd/b/Boudraa:Abdel=Ouahab"},{"title":"(PDF) EMD-Based Signal Filtering","url":"https://www.academia.edu/17726709/EMD_Based_Signal_Filtering"},{"title":"(PDF) EMD-Based Signal Noise Reduction","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/228999069_EMD-Based_Signal_Noise_Reduction"},{"title":"[PDF] EMD-Based Signal Filtering | Semantic Scholar","url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/EMD-Based-Signal-Filtering-Boudraa-Cexus/e4d3324e318ed6531ebe8d0d03b0fbe94ad6fba3"},{"title":"Application of a variation of empirical mode decomposition and teager energy operator to EEG signals for mental task classification | ScienceGate","url":"https://www.sciencegate.app/document/10.1109/embc.2013.6609663"},{"title":"Ensemble Empirical Mode Decomposition-Based Teager Energy Spectrum for Bearing Fault Diagnosis | Journal of Vibration and Acoustics | ASME Digital Collection","url":"https://asmedigitalcollection.asme.org/vibrationacoustics/article-abstract/135/3/031013/472379/Ensemble-Empirical-Mode-Decomposition-Based-Teager?redirectedFrom=fulltext"},{"title":"(PDF) Nonstationary signals analysis by Teager-Huang Transform (THT)","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/47760351_Nonstationary_signals_analysis_by_Teager-Huang_Transform_THT"},{"title":"Multicomponent AM–FM signals analysis based on EMD–B-splines ESA - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0165168412000692"},{"title":"(PDF) EMD-Based signal filtering","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220409465_EMD-Based_signal_filtering"},{"title":"(PDF) Signal detection based on empirical mode decomposition and Teager–Kaiser energy operator and its application to P and S wave arrival time detection in seismic signal analysis","url":"https://www.academia.edu/38207719/Signal_detection_based_on_empirical_mode_decomposition_and_Teager_Kaiser_energy_operator_and_its_application_to_P_and_S_wave_arrival_time_detection_in_seismic_signal_analysis"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about the paper you're looking for:\n\nThe paper \"EMD-Based Signal Filtering\" by Abdel-Ouahab Boudraa and Jean-Christophe Cexus was published in IEEE Transactions on Instrumentation and Measurement, volume 56, issue 6, pages 2196-2202 in 2007.\n\nThe paper proposes a method using partial reconstructions of the signal with relevant Intrinsic Mode Functions (IMFs) corresponding to the most important structures of the signal, with a criterion to determine when the energy distribution of important signal structures overcomes that of noise and high-frequency components.\n\nHowever, the search results do not provide the specific DOI number for this publication. To obtain the complete DOI, you may want to search directly on IEEE Xplore or the paper's direct publication page."],"durationSeconds":7.702070749999999,"searchCount":1}}
