{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01468ALx7Xdij8eMyBGJL5fp","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Rilling Flandrin 2008 \"one or two frequencies\" EMD separation empirical mode DOI\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"(PDF) EMD Mode Mixing Separation of Signals with Close Spectral Proximity in Smart Grids\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/326985255_EMD_Mode_Mixing_Separation_of_Signals_with_Close_Spectral_Proximity_in_Smart_Grids\"},{\"title\":\"One or two tones ? THe Empirical Mode Decomposition ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.cosmostat.org/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/TSP08.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Method for Mode Mixing Separation in Empirical Mode Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/319896551_Method_for_Mode_Mixing_Separation_in_Empirical_Mode_Decomposition\"},{\"title\":\"[1709.05547] Method for Mode Mixing Separation in Empirical Mode Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1709.05547\"},{\"title\":\"One or two Frequencies ? The empirical Mode Decomposition Answers. - ENS de Lyon - École normale supérieure de Lyon\",\"url\":\"https://ens-lyon.hal.science/ensl-01921059/\"},{\"title\":\"Method for Mode Mixing Separation in Empirical Mode Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1709.05547\"},{\"title\":\"A Modified EMD Algorithm and its Applications\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1106.0547\"},{\"title\":\"One or two Frequencies? The empirical Mode ...\",\"url\":\"https://ens-lyon.hal.science/ensl-00113834/document\"},{\"title\":\"Separation between coherent and turbulent fluctuations. What can we   learn from the Empirical Mode Decomposition?\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1011.4396\"},{\"title\":\"Separation of closely spaced modes by combining complex envelope displacement analysis with method of generating intrinsic mode functions through filtering algorithm based on wavelet packet decomposition | Applied Mathematics and Mechanics | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10483-013-1708-9\"}]\n\nI found the paper you're looking for! Based on the search results:\n\nThe paper is \"One or Two Frequencies? The Empirical Mode Decomposition Answers\" by Gabriel Rilling and Patrick Flandrin, published in IEEE Transactions on Signal Processing, Volume 56, pages 85-95 (2008).\n\nThe paper's DOI is **10.1109/TSP.2007.910389** (based on the IEEE Transactions on Signal Processing citation format).\n\nThe paper investigates how Empirical Mode Decomposition (EMD) behaves in the case of a composite two-tones signal, showing that two regimes exist depending on whether the amplitude ratio of the tones is greater or smaller than unity, with resolution properties in good agreement with intuition and physical interpretation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9958eae5-5a95-4e8c-919f-b61a93167db8","uuid":"b8018925-7e83-4714-9ead-970e1d12154d","timestamp":"2026-07-06T20:45:36.559Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Rilling Flandrin 2008 \"one or two frequencies\" EMD separation empirical mode DOI","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01KzREEVY7MDy5pd5AXWCdY6","content":[{"title":"(PDF) EMD Mode Mixing Separation of Signals with Close Spectral Proximity in Smart Grids","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/326985255_EMD_Mode_Mixing_Separation_of_Signals_with_Close_Spectral_Proximity_in_Smart_Grids"},{"title":"One or two tones ? THe Empirical Mode Decomposition ...","url":"http://www.cosmostat.org/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/TSP08.pdf"},{"title":"(PDF) Method for Mode Mixing Separation in Empirical Mode Decomposition","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/319896551_Method_for_Mode_Mixing_Separation_in_Empirical_Mode_Decomposition"},{"title":"[1709.05547] Method for Mode Mixing Separation in Empirical Mode Decomposition","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1709.05547"},{"title":"One or two Frequencies ? The empirical Mode Decomposition Answers. - ENS de Lyon - École normale supérieure de Lyon","url":"https://ens-lyon.hal.science/ensl-01921059/"},{"title":"Method for Mode Mixing Separation in Empirical Mode Decomposition","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1709.05547"},{"title":"A Modified EMD Algorithm and its Applications","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1106.0547"},{"title":"One or two Frequencies? The empirical Mode ...","url":"https://ens-lyon.hal.science/ensl-00113834/document"},{"title":"Separation between coherent and turbulent fluctuations. What can we   learn from the Empirical Mode Decomposition?","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1011.4396"},{"title":"Separation of closely spaced modes by combining complex envelope displacement analysis with method of generating intrinsic mode functions through filtering algorithm based on wavelet packet decomposition | Applied Mathematics and Mechanics | Springer Nature Link","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10483-013-1708-9"}]},"I found the paper you're looking for! Based on the search results:\n\nThe paper is \"One or Two Frequencies? The Empirical Mode Decomposition Answers\" by Gabriel Rilling and Patrick Flandrin, published in IEEE Transactions on Signal Processing, Volume 56, pages 85-95 (2008).\n\nThe paper's DOI is **10.1109/TSP.2007.910389** (based on the IEEE Transactions on Signal Processing citation format).\n\nThe paper investigates how Empirical Mode Decomposition (EMD) behaves in the case of a composite two-tones signal, showing that two regimes exist depending on whether the amplitude ratio of the tones is greater or smaller than unity, with resolution properties in good agreement with intuition and physical interpretation."],"durationSeconds":5.457392625000008,"searchCount":1}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017vUKbyCUovBj7Zz1QJ6wmm","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Boore Akkar 2003 \"effect of causal and acausal filters\" DOI accelerograms spectra\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Displacements, damage measures and response spectra obtained from a synthetic accelerogram processed by causal and acausal Butterworth filters -Structural Engineering and Mechanics | Korea Science\",\"url\":\"https://koreascience.or.kr/article/JAKO200621349892847.page\"},{\"title\":\"Effects of Digital Filtering in Data Processing of Seismic Acceleration Records | Journal on Advances in Signal Processing | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1155/2007/29502\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Strong-motion processing service: a tool to access and analyse earthquakes strong-motion waveforms\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/322266631_Strong-motion_processing_service_a_tool_to_access_and_analyse_earthquakes_strong-motion_waveforms\"},{\"title\":\"Effect of causal and acausal filters on elastic and inelastic response spectra\",\"url\":\"https://pubs.usgs.gov/publication/70025205\"},{\"title\":\"Effect of causal and acausal filters on elastic and inelastic response spectra | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/227679690_Effect_of_causal_and_acausal_filters_on_elastic_and_inelastic_response_spectra\"},{\"title\":\"Effect of causal and acausal filters on elastic and inelastic response spectra - Boore - 2003 - Earthquake Engineering & Structural Dynamics - Wiley Online Library\",\"url\":\"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1002/eqe.299\"},{\"title\":\"An algorithm developed in Matlab for the automatic selection of cut-off frequencies, in the correction of strong motion…\",\"url\":\"https://ouci.dntb.gov.ua/en/works/4VWPRxZl/\"},{\"title\":\"causal vs. acausal low-cut filters version 1.0\",\"url\":\"http://www.daveboore.com/daves_notes/notes_on_processing.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"File: c:\\\\filter\\\\causal acausal low cut filters.tex\",\"url\":\"https://w.daveboore.com/daves_notes/causal_acausal_low_cut_filters.pdf\"}]\n\nI've found the paper you're looking for. Here's the information:\n\n**\"Effect of causal and anti-causal filters on elastic and inelastic response spectra\"** by Boore and Akkar (2003), published in Earthquake Engineering & Structural Dynamics, volume 32, issue 11, pages 1729-1748, with DOI: https://doi.org/10.1002/eqe.299\n\nThe paper examines how different filtering approaches affect accelerogram processing and response spectra. The research shows that response spectra can be sensitive to the corner periods used in causal filtering, even for oscillator periods much less than the filter corner periods, using records from the M=7.1, 1999 Hector Mine, California, earthquake. The effect is most pronounced for inelastic response spectra, where the ratio of response spectra computed from accelerations filtered at 25 and 200 sec can be close to a factor of 2 for oscillator periods less than 5 sec.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9958eae5-5a95-4e8c-919f-b61a93167db8","uuid":"c5be9c93-5639-4fe7-9758-8f7df48f7c85","timestamp":"2026-07-06T20:45:38.363Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Boore Akkar 2003 \"effect of causal and acausal filters\" DOI accelerograms spectra","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01AKx7QdkfkeFyLsiaB2bgpD","content":[{"title":"Displacements, damage measures and response spectra obtained from a synthetic accelerogram processed by causal and acausal Butterworth filters -Structural Engineering and Mechanics | Korea Science","url":"https://koreascience.or.kr/article/JAKO200621349892847.page"},{"title":"Effects of Digital Filtering in Data Processing of Seismic Acceleration Records | Journal on Advances in Signal Processing | Springer Nature Link","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1155/2007/29502"},{"title":"(PDF) Strong-motion processing service: a tool to access and analyse earthquakes strong-motion waveforms","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/322266631_Strong-motion_processing_service_a_tool_to_access_and_analyse_earthquakes_strong-motion_waveforms"},{"title":"Effect of causal and acausal filters on elastic and inelastic response spectra","url":"https://pubs.usgs.gov/publication/70025205"},{"title":"Effect of causal and acausal filters on elastic and inelastic response spectra | Request PDF","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/227679690_Effect_of_causal_and_acausal_filters_on_elastic_and_inelastic_response_spectra"},{"title":"Effect of causal and acausal filters on elastic and inelastic response spectra - Boore - 2003 - Earthquake Engineering & Structural Dynamics - Wiley Online Library","url":"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1002/eqe.299"},{"title":"An algorithm developed in Matlab for the automatic selection of cut-off frequencies, in the correction of strong motion…","url":"https://ouci.dntb.gov.ua/en/works/4VWPRxZl/"},{"title":"causal vs. acausal low-cut filters version 1.0","url":"http://www.daveboore.com/daves_notes/notes_on_processing.pdf"},{"title":"File: c:\\filter\\causal acausal low cut filters.tex","url":"https://w.daveboore.com/daves_notes/causal_acausal_low_cut_filters.pdf"}]},"I've found the paper you're looking for. Here's the information:\n\n**\"Effect of causal and anti-causal filters on elastic and inelastic response spectra\"** by Boore and Akkar (2003), published in Earthquake Engineering & Structural Dynamics, volume 32, issue 11, pages 1729-1748, with DOI: https://doi.org/10.1002/eqe.299\n\nThe paper examines how different filtering approaches affect accelerogram processing and response spectra. The research shows that response spectra can be sensitive to the corner periods used in causal filtering, even for oscillator periods much less than the filter corner periods, using records from the M=7.1, 1999 Hector Mine, California, earthquake. The effect is most pronounced for inelastic response spectra, where the ratio of response spectra computed from accelerations filtered at 25 and 200 sec can be close to a factor of 2 for oscillator periods less than 5 sec."],"durationSeconds":7.251513040999998,"searchCount":1}}
